# Application Kconfig.
#
# One symbol so far. It exists rather than being implied by CONFIG_LORA
# because "the board has a LoRa radio" and "this firmware should announce
# itself on a mesh" are different decisions — a RAK4631 flown somewhere with
# no MeshCore network wants the driver's flash back.

config APP_LORA_STATUS
	bool "Announce DFU progress on a MeshCore channel over LoRa"
	depends on LORA
	default y
	help
	  Mirrors the dfu_status record onto a MeshCore group channel: the
	  target found, progress at 25/50/75%, verification, and the outcome.
	  Transmit only — there is no receive path and the device is not a
	  mesh node.

	  Only the RAK4631 has the radio. On every other board CONFIG_LORA is
	  off, this is unselectable, and lora_status.h's empty inlines make
	  the call sites in dfu_status.c disappear.

	  The channel is set in config.txt (`lora_channel`), and an empty
	  value there keeps the radio idle without rebuilding.

source "Kconfig.zephyr"
